    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "the \"helplines\" just don't get it. they're just scripts. they don't get that when you're socially dead, there's literally no path back. there's no \"holding space\" for someone who has nothing left to offer. it feels like i'm just a burden that everyone is collectively waiting to see disappear. if i'm already dead to everyone else, what's even the point of staying around to watch it happen?",
